"""A mostly near-zero signal, with negative responses to script-openers.

A caret or underscore introducing a braced exponent/subscript is strongly
negative; other carets are weaker. The previous token handles split openers.
Repeated opening brackets and quote-and-brace openings are weaker.
Carriage-return line endings are also negative, but fade with repetition in a
document. Conversation/tool/thinking delimiters have their own small offsets.
These rules summarize recurring high-importance punctuation patterns rather
than assigning an arbitrary learned value to every ordinary word.
